# The Dark Side of the Light (DSOTL) — product vision (PO lock)

**Owner:** Marcin / Noir Frame. This is an **authorial vernissage**, not a generic feature or Easter egg playground.

## Non‑negotiable name and idea

- The project is **The Dark Side of the Light** (DSOTL).
- Do **not** rename, merge into “blog”, replace with clock toys, or reinterpret as a generic dark mode / gimmick.
- If a change **contradicts this document**, stop and push back — explain why it breaks PO intent before implementing alternatives.

## Two separate things (do not conflate)

### 1. Moon on `noirframe.art` (main menu)

- **Only** a **bonus video** (material in production).
- Flow: click moon → play bonus video → **return to main menu**. End.
- No gallery, no labyrinth, no extra scenes on the main site beyond that video (unless PO explicitly updates this rule).
- Prototype code (clock, fade paths) is **temporary** until the bonus video ships; then simplify to video → menu.

### 2. DSOTL (full experience)

- A **specially modified Noir Frame engine** — separate from the casual moon click on the public menu.
- Opens a **strong gallery / vernissage**: curated author exhibition, not portfolio tiles.
- Content policy: **no violence, no pedophilia, no pornography** — artistic, author-controlled work only.

## Implementation guardrails

- Do not expand moon click into DSOTL gallery on the same URL without PO approval.
- Do not add social features, likes, or CMS scope to DSOTL unless PO requests it.
- Prefer `DARK_SIDE_ENABLED` / feature flags until DSOTL engine and assets are ready.
- When implementing DSOTL engine, treat it as its own module or fork — not a patch on Contact/Portfolio geometry.

